{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Jacob told Rachel that he was her father's brother.</b> And afterward, 'and Jacob kissed Rachel.' Another interpretation: 'And Jacob told Rachel that he was her father's brother' — so that she would not be disdained for the fact that he kissed her. 'And she told her father' — because he had told her that he was her father's brother. But regarding Rebekah, since she did not know who he was, it is written 'and she told her mother' — for daughters are normally found with their mothers."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:34.129356845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}